  "description": "QOVBIP crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H99 Dy12 N27 O78,C6 H15 N1,3(C2 H3 N1),9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.490-4.049 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.13-116.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy12(H2ovih)3(μ3-O)9(H2O)24(NO3)9]·2C6H15N·3C2H3N·9H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 9 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 24 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
